                    <body>
                    <center>
                    <table width='600' border='0' cellspacing='0' cellpadding='20'>
                      <tr>
                        <td><h3>Version: TDSMAN 15.02</h3>
                          <h3>Version Date: 26th April 2014</h3>
                          <h3>Released on: 26th April 2014</h3>
                          <h2>New FVU Versions 4.2 and 2.138 is  now incorporated with the following changes</h2>
                          <ul>
                            <li>Nil challans will be permitted with no deductee  records for Form 24Q Q4</li>
                            <li>Mandatory to deduct TDS at 20% or more for Form  No. 24Q where employee is marked with Higher Deduction flag i.e. &ldquo;C&rdquo;</li>
                            <li>Value for Form 15CA, required for Form 27Q  deductees, can have alphanumeric characters between 12 to 15 characters. </li>
                          </ul>
                          <h2>Bulk PAN Verification facility  added for Professional Edition</h2>
                          <p>Users will now be able to verify all the PANs present in the  statement. This process involves checking of each PAN with Income Tax  Department&rsquo;s database and intimating all the invalid PANs.</p>
                              <h2>&ldquo;Interest Allocated&rdquo; and &ldquo;Other Allocated&rdquo;  of Challan details in Add mode through Preference</h2>
                            <p>Users can now opt to show through Interest Allocated field  and Others Allocated field of Challan Details while adding new records. This  was previously shown while modifying the existing record only.</p>
                      <h2>List of Previous updates can be seen from  Utilities Menu</h2>
                            <p>Users can now see list of all the updates done in the  software by clicking on &ldquo;View Previous Updates&rdquo; option available on Utilities  Menu</p>
                      <h2>Direct Download link provided for TDS  Certificate and Default converter</h2>
                            <p>Users can now directly download the TDS Converter and  Defaults converter which are required to convert the respective files  downloaded from TRACES by clicking on the &ldquo;Traces Information&rdquo; menu.</p>
                      <h2>The correction option for additional Salary  Details now provided</h2>
                            <p>The correction option for additional Salary details which  requires breakup current and previous employers Taxable Income and Tax is now  provided.</p>
                          <h2>Other Bug Fixes</h2>
                          <ul>
                            <li>Search and Filter problems in Reports</li>
                            <li>Check provided for 1,00,000 lack limit of 80C</li>
                            <li>Bugs in Short Deduction calculation for Firm  Deductees</li>
                            <li>File Download problems in TRACES</li>
                          </ul>
                          <p><strong><span class='style1'>Fine Tunings</strong></p>
                          <ul>
                            <li>Option to open the relevant Form directly after  Excel import and TDS file import.</li>
		                    <li> Copying text file generated to the Output Folder  of the return</li>
                          </ul>
                         </td>
                      </tr>
                    </table>
                    </center>
                    </body>
                    </html>";
                            #endregion
