                                        <td><h3>Version: TDSMAN 15.28</h3>
                                          <h3>Version Date: 26th September  2014</h3>
                                          <h3>Released on: 26th September  2014</h3>
                                          <h2>Professional Edition deductee  limit increased to 5,00,000</h2>
                                          <p>In TDSMAN&rsquo;s Professional edition  the deductee limit has been increased to 5,00,000.</p>
                                          <h3>Changes as per new rules  introduced in FVU 4.4</h3>
                                          <h2>197 Certificate Validation</h2>
                                          <p>Valid 197 certificate number has  to be provided, wherever applicable.</p>
                                          <h2>Salary Amount entry restricted to  Rs. 99,99,99,999</h2>
                                          <p>Salary amount entry cannot exceed Rs. 99 crores in employee  detail entry as well as salary details entry.</p>
                                          <h2>Alloting Deductee Reference No. /  Employee Serial number for deductees without PANs</h2>
                                          <p>Software now automatically allots deductee reference number  for deductees without PANs. User also has the option to manually provide this  reference number in the Deductee / Employee master. The return report has been  modified accordingly to reflect this new field.</p>
                                              <h2>AIN number is now mandatory  for Central &amp; State Government Deductors</h2><br>

                                          <h2>Collection code &ldquo;J&rdquo; &amp; &ldquo;K&rdquo; now  valid only from Q2 of FY 2012-13</h2>
                                          <p>Collection code &ldquo;J&rdquo; and &ldquo;K&rdquo; is applicable pertaining to Q2  of FY 2012-13 onwards. If this is used for earlier periods, while generating  returns, FVU will show the error.</p>
                                          <h2>Higher Rate &ldquo;C&rdquo; flag valid only  for missing PANs</h2>
                                          <p>Remarks for higher deduction in deductee details i.e., flag  &ldquo;C&rdquo; to be mentioned only if the deductee PAN is missing.<a name='_GoBack'></a></p>
                                          <h2>Country Name &ldquo;Mexico&rdquo; changed to  &ldquo;UNITED MEXICAN STATES&rdquo;</h2>
                                        </td>
