                                        <body>
                                        <table width='600' border='0' cellspacing='0' cellpadding='20'>
                                        <tbody><tr>
                                        <td><h3>Version: TDSMAN 16.12</h3>
                                          <h3>Version Date: 7th April 2015</h3>
                                          <h3>Released on: 7th April 2015</h3>										                                            
                                          <ol>
                                            <li><u>Provision to enter deductee entries without  challan</u></li>                                         
                                          <p>Users can now  enter deductees before entering its challan payment. These deductees can later  be tagged to its challan. </p>                                          
                                            <li><u>Provision to upgrade to Multi User</u></li>                                          
                                          <p>TDSMAN can now  be updated to Multi user environment at an additional cost. This feature is  available Financial Year 2015-16 onwards.</p>                                          
                                            <li><u>Provision to block a company for return entry</u></li>                                          
                                          <p>Users can now  block a company (TAN) so that it doesn&rsquo;t appear for return preparation.  However, <a name='_GoBack'></a>reports of this company can be viewed.</p>                                          
                                            <li><u>Salary Details module optimized</u></li>
											<p>Salary details  module has been optimized to handle Current Employer and Previous Employer&rsquo;s  breakup in better way.</p>
                                          </ol>
                                          <h2>&nbsp;</h2>
                                          </td>
                                        </tr>
                                        </tbody></table>    
                                        </body></html>
                                        ";
