                                          <h2>TDSMAN has been updated to support FVU 4.6 & FVU 2.142 for preparation of returns</h2>
                                          <p> The following are important in this update: </p>
					                        <p>Regular Returns :</p>
					                      <ol>
                                          <li>PAN of the Responsible Person is mandatory.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 27Q applicable list of Nature of Remittance has been reduced.</li>
                                          <li>Mandatory quoting of BIN Details from FY 13-14 onwards(only for Govt. deductors).</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCE has been updated to Rs. 1,50,000 for FY 14-15 onwards.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCF should be equal to or less than Rs. 20,000 for FY 10-11 & 11-					                      12.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCG should be equal to or less than Rs. 25,000 for FY 12-13                      		                      onwards.</li>                                 
					                      </ol> 
				                              <p>Correction Returns :</p>
                                          <ol>
                                          <li>PAN of the Responsible Person is mandatory for Correction returns.</li>
                                          <li>Mandatory quoting of BIN Details from FY 13-14 onwards(only for Govt. deductors).</li>
                                          <li>Tax Deposit amount can be modified for records where tax has been deducted at higher rate.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCE has been updated to Rs. 1,50,000 for FY 14-15 onwards.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCF should be equal to or less than Rs. 20,000 for FY 10-11 & 11-12.</li>
                                          <li>In Form 24Q deduction under section 80CCG should be equal to or less than Rs. 25,000 for FY 12-13 onwards.</li>                                          
                                          </ol> 
