                                        <body>
                                            <table style='margin: auto; border: solid 1px black;' width='800' border='0' cellspacing='0'
                                                cellpadding='20'>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>
                                                        <img style='display: block; margin: auto' src='http://www.tdsman.com/images/tdsman-logo-header.png' />
                                                        <h1>
                                                            Update document for Version 16.18</h1>
                                                        <h3>
                                                            Version: TDSMAN 16.18</h3>
                                                        <h3>
                                                            Version Date: 30th September 2015</h3>
                                                        <h3>
                                                            Released on: 30th September 2015</h3>
                                                        <h2 style='font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px'>
                                                            Changes made as per FVU 4.8 & FVU 2.144</h2>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Incorporation of section 192A in Form No. 27Q</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            Section 192A, which was earlier introduced in Form No. 26Q for EPF payments made,
                                                            is now applicable in Form No. 27Q as well.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Discontinuation in addition of challan in Correction return
                                                        </h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            As per the new rules of the department, challans cannot be added in correction
                                                            returns. Addition of challans can be done by Online correction mechanism present
                                                            in TRACES website</p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Removal of some nature of Remittance in Form 27Q</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            The following nature of remittance has been removed:
                                                        </p>
                                                        <ul>
                                                            <li>Commission </li>
                                                            <li>Payments to sports person & artists </li>
                                                            <li>Winning from horse races</li>
                                                            <li>Winning from lotteries, crossword puzzles, card games and other games of any sort</li>
                                                        </ul>
                                                        <h2 style='font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px'>
                                                            Other Changes</h2>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Grossing up Indicator in form 27Q</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            Grossing up indicator has been provided in form 27Q.</p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Late deduction Calculation</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            In Predict Defaults section, software will now also check whether any late TDS deduction
                                                            was done and will accordingly calculate its applicable interests.</p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Create Company Master from any TDS File</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            In 'Import from TDS file' module option has been provided to create any new company
                                                            record by importing data from that company's TDS file.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Restore any modified record in correction</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            Facility has been provided to restore any modified record to its original values
                                                            in correction. To restore any modified record, select the particular record from
                                                            the grid and click on 'Restore' button.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Import Salary details in corrections using excel</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            Salary details can now be imported from excel in correction returns.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Generate separate PDF for each certificate</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            Facility has been provided to generate separate PDF for each certificate (Form 16,
                                                            16A, 27D).
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Option to Merge TRACES's Form 16 part A with Form 16 part B</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            While generating Form 16 part B report, one now has the provision of merging the
                                                            generated report with department's generated Form 16 part A certificate.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <h2>
                                                            Multiple requests from TRACES module</h2>
                                                        <p>
                                                            One can now place multiple file requests from TRACES module. For example - While
                                                            requesting Conso file for any return, you can also request for its certificate file
                                                            and justification report file.
                                                        </p>
                                                        <hr />
                                                    </td>
                                                </tr>
                                            </table>
                                        </body>
                                        </html>";
