							                            <h2 style='font-weight:bold'>
                                                            Changes made as per FVU 5.4 & FVU 2.150. 
                                                        </h2>
				                                        <br /><br />
				                                        <p>
					                                    The new FVUs have been released by the Income Tax Department on 23rd Feb 2017 and is also made applicable from the same date onwards.
				                                        </p>                                                        
                                                        
                                                        <p>TDSMAN is being updated to take care of all the announced changes. 
							</h2>
	                                                <p />
							<p>
							Validation for 'PAN of Landlord' field has been revised for form 24Q-Q4 under
							Annexure II (i.e. Salary details) from F.Y. 2016-17 onwards.
								 Existing Validation of structurally valid PAN (for field no. 41, 43, 45 and 47 as per
							data structure) has been relaxed. These fields may contain any value from the below
							mentioned when the landlord does not have PAN.
							<li> GOVERNMENT: This is applicable when landlords are Government
								organizations (i.e. Central or State).</li>
							<li> NONRESDENT: This is applicable when the landlords are Non-Residents.</li>
							<li> OTHERVALUE: This is applicable when the landlords are other than
							Government organization and Non-Residents.</li>

							</p>    
	                                                </br>
							<h2 style='font-weight:bold'>
                                                            Introduction of Reference No. for Form 26Q and Form 27Q
                                                        </h2>
							<p>There is a provision for reference number of each deductee record which also reflects in the TDS Certificate (Form 16A). TDSMAN has introduced the facility for using this provision by entering the transaction reference number against each deductee record. To get this activated, it needs to be set up through 'Utilities - Preferences'. This facility has also been incorporated in the excel import.<p/>
							<h2 style='font-weight:bold'>
                                                            Challan Balance in the interface of Correction Returns 
                                                        </h2>
							<p>The Conso / TDS file carries the unutilized amount for each relevant Challan. This information is now being displayed Correction Return interface.<p/>
							<h2 style='font-weight:bold'>
                                                            Excel import facility for Salary Details (Form 16 - details)
                                                        </h2>
							<p>Till now, one could import through Excel the Salary Details to the extent that was required for filing the TDS Returns for Form 24Q-Q4. The Part-A of the Form 16 is provided by the IT Department based on this information filed by the Employer. The information pertaining to Part B of Form 16 is to be entered manually (for printing Form 16 - Part B). For Professional & Enterprise users of TDSMAN, facility of excel import of these details has been incorporated.<p/>
							</td>
                                                </tr>
                                            </table>
                                        </body>
                                        </html>";
