                                                        <br/>                                                
							                            <h2 style='font-weight:bold'>Introduction of TDSMAN Dashboard</h2></h2>	<br/> 	
														<p>On popular demand, a Dashboard has been introduced which provides a summary of the following:</p>													
														<li>List of TDS / TCS Returns under process of being prepared</li>
														<li>List of TDS / TCS Returns is ready for Filing (FVU has been generated)</li>
														<li>List of TDS / TCS Returns that has been filed (Token / Receipt No. has been updated)</li>
														<li>Status of Returns across all quarters of a Financial Year</li><br/>
														<p>Click on the 'Go to Dashboard' link on the top right of the Home Screen. 
														This will direct you to the Dashboard. On the dashboard, there is an option 
														to make this the default Landing Screen. At any point once on exiting the Dashboard, 
														it is redirected back to the Home Screen.</p>
														<p>Directly from the Dashboard, one can click and access the Return.</p>														
														<br/>                         
														<h2 style='font-weight:bold'>Salary & TDS Summary Report</h2></h2>	<br/> 			                                                                                      
														<p>In the quarterly Returns (Form 24Q), the details of the Salary and TDS is provided for each employee as relevant for the quarter. 
														This applies to all four quarters. In the last quarter, in Annexure II, 
														the detailed tax computation of each employee needs to be provided which ultimately forms the basis of Form 16.</p>
														<p>This new 'Salary & TDS Summary Report' provides a one line summary of each employee for the Salary & TDS for 
														each quarter and that reported in Annexure II. The sum total of all four quarters is compared with the figures in Annexure II. 
														However, in case of any mismatch, the same is highlighted. This report may be helpful, to weed out any exceptions.</p>															   
                                                                     </br>
																	 <p>
							                            Reported bugs rectified.
							                            </p>
