                                                        </h3>
                                                        <h3>
                                                            Released Date: 02nd February 2023
                                                        </h3>     
                                                        <br/>   
														<h2><b>This is the launch of TDSMAN (FY:23-24)</b></h2>														
							                            <p>Throughout the course of the last one year, progressively, our team has been closely tracking the statutory changes and have been regularly updating the software. A lot of new sections have been introduced which has all been incorporated.<br/>
														<p>Summary of some important developments are as under:<br/>
														<h2>TDSMAN – now in 'Full Screen'</h2>														
							                            <p>The software had been developed for a particular screen resolution which at that point of time was using the entire visible space. However, over the course of last 8-10 years, the screen resolution has substantially increased and as a consequence, the software only occupied a part of the screen. TDSMAN has now been updated so that it would dynamically adapt to the user's screen resolution for a full screen display. Hope this would provide a better experience.<br/>
														<h2>NSDL / TRACES / Income Tax Integration</h2>														
							                            <p>Throughout the last 12 months, the Income Tax Department has been making substantial changes within their own technology infrastructure with a gradual shift of quite a few facilities to the new Income Tax portal from the existing NSDL and TRACES. Our team, despite many hurdles are trying to keep pace with the integration related changes. Using TDSMAN, now the interface integration for TDS / TCS Return Filing, Downloading of CSI, etc. has been successfully implemented.<br/>
														<h2>Dashboard</h2>														
							                            <p>This has been a recent introduction wherein from a single interface, one can access all the TDS / TCS Returns. It includes Returns that are ‘Under Process', ‘Ready for Filing', ‘Filed Returns' & ‘Filing Status'. This ‘Dashboard' can be accessed from a link on the ‘Home Screen'. As an option, one can have the ‘Dashboard' as the default ‘Home Screen'.<br/>
														<h2>CSV Import</h2>														
							                            <p>Importing data from Excel has always been available in TDSMAN. On popular demand, as an option, at most places, now import from CSV has also been introduced. Not only CSV is a popular generic text file format but the speed of data import is at least 25% faster. In Excel and other spreadsheet software, most have the option to ‘Save' the file in CSV format.<br/>
														<br>Reported bugs rectified.<br/>
							                                         </br>
                                                                 </br><a href = 'https://blog.tdsman.com/' > Click here </a> to view TDSMAN blog.
                                                                      </td>
                                                                      </tr>
                                                                  </table>
                                                              </body>
                                                              </html>";
